<% content_for :title, "Privacy · Nuclear Directory" %>
<% content_for :head do %>
  <meta name="description" content="What Nuclear Directory records: page views, searches, time on page and dead clicks, the country you're visiting from, and what you type into a correction. No accounts, no advertising trackers, one security cookie.">
<% end %>
<%= render "shared/site_header" %>

<main class="nd-page nd-page--narrow nd-prose">
  <h1 class="type-title-md">Privacy</h1>
  <p class="type-body-strong">Nuclear Directory doesn't ask who you are.</p>
  <p class="type-body">There are no accounts and no advertising trackers.</p>

  <section aria-labelledby="cookie">
    <h2 id="cookie" class="type-body-strong">One cookie, for form security</h2>
    <p class="type-body">It protects the site's forms against forged submissions and ends when you close your browser.</p>
    <p class="type-small text-ink-muted">It holds no information about you and isn't used to count or follow visits.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="counts">
    <h2 id="counts" class="type-body-strong">We count how the site is used, without cookies</h2>
    <p class="type-body">We use PostHog to count page views, searches, how long a page stays open and dead clicks. Nothing is stored in your browser, and one visit isn't linked to the next.</p>
    <ul class="type-small text-ink-muted">
      <li>Searches are recorded with their words and how many results they found.</li>
      <li>A dead click is a click on something that doesn't respond, such as text that looks like a link. It's recorded with the text of what was clicked.</li>
      <li>Page addresses are recorded without their query strings.</li>
      <li>There are no session recordings and no visitor accounts.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="ip">
    <h2 id="ip" class="type-body-strong">We keep your country, not your IP address</h2>
    <p class="type-body">We look up which country you're in from your IP address, on this site's server, and add only the country to the analytics data.</p>
    <p class="type-body">PostHog also receives your IP address and browser with each request, to count unique visitors without cookies, and doesn't store the IP address.</p>
    <p class="type-small text-ink-muted">The country data is <a class="nd-link" href="https://db-ip.com">IP Geolocation by DB-IP</a>, used under the <a class="nd-link" href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a> license.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="relay">
    <h2 id="relay" class="type-body-strong">Analytics go through this site</h2>
    <p class="type-body">PostHog's scripts, and the data they send, go through this site rather than straight to PostHog.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="corrections">
    <h2 id="corrections" class="type-body-strong">A correction keeps what you type, to reply to you</h2>
    <p class="type-body">We keep your message, the page it's about and, if you add one, your email address. We use your email only to reply about that correction.</p>
    <p class="type-small text-ink-muted">We don't store your IP address with it. To stop floods of reports, a scrambled form of your IP address is kept in the site's cache for ten minutes and then deleted.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="errors">
    <h2 id="errors" class="type-body-strong">Error reports leave you out</h2>
    <p class="type-body">When a page fails, an error report goes to Sentry with the page address and the error.</p>
    <p class="type-small text-ink-muted">It leaves out cookies, form contents, query strings and anything that identifies you.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="hosting">
    <h2 id="hosting" class="type-body-strong">Hosting on Render</h2>
    <p class="type-body">Fonts and scripts are served from this site, not from a third party.</p>
    <p class="type-small text-ink-muted">Like any web host, Render keeps standard server logs, which include IP addresses, for a limited time to run and secure the service.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="contact">
    <h2 id="contact" class="type-body-strong">Questions</h2>
    <p class="type-body">Email <%= mail_to DirectoryHelper::CORRECTIONS_EMAIL, nil, class: "nd-link" %>.</p>
  </section>

  <p class="type-small text-ink-muted">Last updated <span class="type-data-sm">2026-10-12</span></p>
</main>
